$ bash bin/fm-dod-lib.sh --help
Usage: bash bin/fm-dod-lib.sh --verification-plan <brief>
       bash bin/fm-dod-lib.sh --shape
Render task DoD, exclusions and the shared review rubric for no-mistakes --verification-plan FILE.
CRLF input is accepted; unreadable or NUL-bearing input stops construction with an error; a present DoD must carry mandatory items in the shape --shape prints; legacy briefs with no DoD state absent criteria and unrecognized exclusions.
--shape prints the mandatory item shape as key=value lines: id, lead, fields, authority_field, authorities, item, rule.
exit=0

$ bash bin/fm-dod-lib.sh --verification-plan idless.md   # old fixture shape "- Source: ..." (no id)
error: verification plan refuses the task Definition Of Done: mandatory item has no id: Expected: x reaches y.
Each mandatory item starts its own line as `<ID> Source: ... Expected: ... Verify: ... Edge/negative: ... Evidence place: ... Authority: ...`, with an id matching `[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*` that is unique within the section and every field nonempty; Authority is exactly agent, gate, or grader.
exit=1

